# Database Migration Anti-Patterns

## DROP TABLE IF EXISTS — data loss

```sql
-- WRONG — all user data gone
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS product;
CREATE TABLE product (...);
```

**Fix: ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN. Preserve existing data.**

## No version tracking — can't determine current schema

```java
// WRONG — no way to know what version DB is on
```

**Fix: schema_version table. Ebean checks it before running migrations.**

## Adding NOT NULL column without default

```sql
-- WRONG — fails on existing rows
ALTER TABLE product ADD COLUMN barcode VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL;
```

**Fix: Add as nullable, backfill data, then set NOT NULL.**

## Testing migration on production database

```java
// WRONG — migrations run on real user data without backup
```

**Fix: Always backup first. Test on a copy in a transaction you can rollback.